---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'; import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro'; import CallToAction from '../../components/CallToAction.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="AI Player Scouting for FM26 | FM AI Assistent" description="Search and compare Football Manager 2026 players using attributes, positions, contracts and finances from your loaded save snapshot." path="/features/scouting/">
  <div class="page-shell"><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'Features',href:'/features/'},{label:'Player scouting'}]} /><header class="page-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Player database</p><h1>Scout and compare players in FM26.</h1><p class="lead">Turn the loaded save into a searchable market. Narrow the database with football and financial filters, inspect each candidate and carry verified IDs into comparisons or shortlists.</p></header>
    <section class="section feature-showcase"><div><h2>Search the database you are actually playing.</h2><p>The app documents filters for ability, potential, age, reputation, nationality, club, competition, position, individual attributes, wages, asking price, contract end, height and gender.</p><ul class="check-list"><li>Sort and filter the full loaded player snapshot</li><li>Inspect visible and hidden attributes exposed by the app</li><li>Review positions, club, contract and financial context</li><li>Compare selected players by FM Unique ID</li></ul></div><figure class="screenshot-frame"><a href="/images/player-filters.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Open the player filter screenshot at full size"><img src="/images/player-filters.png" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" alt="FM AI Assistent filter dialog for narrowing the loaded player database" /></a><figcaption><span>The real filter workflow used to narrow player candidates.</span><a href="/images/player-filters.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View full size ↗</a></figcaption></figure></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">A repeatable workflow</p><h2>How do I compare replacements?</h2></div><p>Start broad, then make the football question explicit before asking the assistant to rank anyone.</p></div><div class="steps"><article class="step"><h3>Define the job</h3><p>Specify position, side, role, age range and constraints.</p></article><article class="step"><h3>Filter locally</h3><p>Use the database to see what exists in this save.</p></article><article class="step"><h3>Inspect evidence</h3><p>Open promising profiles and check cost and contract gaps.</p></article><article class="step"><h3>Compare IDs</h3><p>Ask the assistant to compare the exact finalists, not name matches.</p></article></div><p class="notice"><strong>Boundary:</strong> a loaded snapshot can become outdated as the career advances. Select <strong>Load data</strong> again when you need current game values.</p></section>
  </div><CallToAction eyebrow="Build your shortlist" title="Start with the official release." />
</BaseLayout>
